<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Conrad II, Count of Dachau</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1159</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Conrad II (d. 1159) was a Bavarian count of Dachau to whom <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a> gave the title Duke of Merania around 1152, making him its first holder. Merania referred to coastal lands on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kvarner-gulf">Kvarner Gulf</a> and in Istria. After the Dachau line died out, the title passed in 1180 to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-andechs">counts of Andechs</a>.</p></div>
